WEBVTT

00:00:01.710 --> 00:00:02.959
Hi, I'm Saltine!

00:00:02.959 --> 00:00:07.953
Kimi K3 moves information along the sequence, across depth, and across experts.

00:00:10.183 --> 00:00:12.807
Three layers in four keep a fixed memory.

00:00:12.807 --> 00:00:14.447
Every fourth attends in full.

00:00:14.447 --> 00:00:17.399
And each layer reads the earlier ones by attention.

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:22.343
Each head keeps a matrix memory.

00:00:22.763 --> 00:00:25.073
First, every channel decays at its own rate.

00:00:25.810 --> 00:00:27.799
Then it erases what it held for this key.

00:00:29.245 --> 00:00:30.609
And writes the new value.

00:00:30.609 --> 00:00:31.973
Only the error gets written.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:38.139
Three KDA layers, then one latent attention layer, twenty-three times, and

00:00:38.139 --> 00:00:39.644
a final global layer.

00:00:40.064 --> 00:00:44.487
Only the twenty-four attention layers grow a cache: one small latent per

00:00:44.487 --> 00:00:46.330
token, with no position encoding.

00:00:47.883 --> 00:00:50.859
A plain residual adds every layer with weight one.

00:00:50.859 --> 00:00:53.505
K3 sums its layers in blocks of twelve.

00:00:53.925 --> 00:00:55.810
Each layer has a learned query.

00:00:55.810 --> 00:00:58.639
It attends over the embedding and every earlier block.

00:00:59.155 --> 00:01:02.645
The softmax weights decide which depths it reads, token by token.

00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:09.778
A sigmoid router scores every expert, with a bias from quantile balancing

00:01:09.778 --> 00:01:11.104
to even the load.

00:01:11.524 --> 00:01:15.069
The token is projected down to half width, and only the top

00:01:15.069 --> 00:01:16.251
sixteen experts run there.

00:01:16.670 --> 00:01:20.380
Their mix is normalised and projected back up, and two shared experts

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:21.617
add a full-width path.

00:01:22.842 --> 00:01:26.647
Twenty-seven kilobytes of cache per token, plus the fixed state.

00:01:26.647 --> 00:01:29.310
A million tokens fit in twenty-seven gigabytes.

00:01:32.142 --> 00:01:36.015
A fixed memory on most layers, exact attention on a quarter, and

00:01:36.015 --> 00:01:37.307
learned reads across depth.

00:01:40.233 --> 00:01:42.120
A delta rule for memory.

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:43.629
Latent attention for recall.

00:01:43.629 --> 00:01:46.648
Attention across depth, and sixteen experts per token.

00:01:47.068 --> 00:01:49.291
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:49.291 --> 00:01:49.926
I'm Saltine.

00:01:49.926 --> 00:01:50.243
Bye!
